## What did not work

In accordance with protocol rules, more complex options were tested against simpler rivals and rejected when failing pre-registered material effect thresholds:

- Stacking versus Ridge: A temporal stacking ensemble (Ridge and Random Forest bases combined with an XGBoost meta-regressor) was ablated against standalone Ridge. On synthetic linear-truth benchmarks, the stacker degraded relative performance by {{reports/harness_stack.json#linear_truth_stack_gain_rel|pct1}}. On the sealed holdout, the challenger {{reports/holdout_results.json#claim_challenger_vs_ridge}} the Ridge baseline. Ridge was retained as the default served model.
- Target Transformation: QuantileTransformer regression was ablated against standard `log1p` transformation. The QuantileTransformer degraded performance with relative loss of {{reports/imbalance_decision.json#target_decision.relative_gain|pct1}} across validation folds (ninety-five percent confidence interval [{{reports/imbalance_decision.json#target_decision.ci_lo|pct1}}, {{reports/imbalance_decision.json#target_decision.ci_hi|pct1}}]), failing across all folds.
- Imbalance Resampling: Synthetic minority oversampling for regression (SMOTER) was tested against standard weighting. SMOTER provided negligible benefit on tail error while increasing bulk variance, leading to its rejection.
- Engineered Feature Controls: Three candidate features were ablated:
  - `price_bucket`: Relative gain {{reports/feature_decision.json#decisions.price_bucket.relative_gain|pct1}}, lower bound below zero; dropped.
  - `high_value_flag`: Relative gain {{reports/feature_decision.json#decisions.high_value_flag.relative_gain|pct1}}, lower bound below zero; dropped.
  - `cat_region_level`: Relative gain {{reports/feature_decision.json#decisions.cat_region_level.relative_gain|pct1}}, below required threshold; dropped.

## Explanations

Interpretability is enforced via exact linear SHAP:

- Primary attribution driver: Feature `{{reports/shap_probe.json#top_feature}}` is the dominant signal with mean absolute SHAP value {{reports/shap_probe.json#top_feature_mean_abs_shap|f4}}.
- Noise probe validation: Random probe features demonstrated minimal attribution, with maximum relative impact of {{reports/shap_probe.json#max_noise_rel_to_top|pct1}} compared to the top feature, and zero noise features in the top tier (exactly {{reports/shap_probe.json#noise_in_top_k|int}} noise features in top ranks).
- Method cross-check: Spearman rank correlation between SHAP attribution and permutation importance reached {{reports/shap_crosscheck.json#spearman_rank_correlation|f4}}, with top rank overlap of {{reports/shap_crosscheck.json#top3_overlap|int}} features.

## API, UI and Docker usage

Run the application locally or via Docker Compose:

```bash
# Start FastAPI service locally
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m uvicorn api.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

# Start Streamlit UI locally
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m streamlit run ui/app.py --server.port 8501

# Run containerized services
docker compose -p revpred-p9 up -d --build

# Run docker smoke verification
bash scripts/docker_smoke.sh
```

FastAPI endpoints include `GET /health`, `GET /meta`, `POST /predict`, and `POST /explain`.

